HARNESS CONTRACT (the gates verify every point below mechanically):

You write ONLY `src/lib.rs`. A fixed, pre-generated `src/main.rs` CLI
shell (and separate fuzz targets) call into it, so lib.rs MUST export
exactly this interface:

  /// (op_name, runner) registry — one entry per operation.
  pub fn ops() -> Vec<(&'static str, fn(&[u8], u64) -> String)>

  /// Write, for EVERY operation with "needs_input": true, exactly two
  /// DISTINCT, VALID input files: <dir>/<op>.1.bin and <dir>/<op>.2.bin
  /// (deterministic bytes — same files on every run). You may call the
  /// library itself to synthesize them (e.g. use the encoder to produce
  /// inputs for a decode operation). Return one line per file:
  /// `seed <op> <path>`.
  pub fn gen_seeds(dir: &str) -> Vec<String>

  /// Write, for each operation whose work SCALES with input size, ONE input
  /// `<dir>/<op>.perf.bin` that is LARGE and REALISTIC enough that the
  /// operation's inner loop — not per-call setup/malloc/memset/libc —
  /// dominates a profiled run (the library's own code should account for the
  /// bulk of the time). This usually needs SEVERAL MEGABYTES, not a few KB.
  ///
  /// The data MUST be REALISTIC for the operation, NOT random/uniform bytes.
  /// Random or degenerate data makes many kernels take a trivial path and stay
  /// cold: compressors/matchers find no repeats, parsers/decoders hit an early
  /// error and bail, searches find nothing. Generate data with the STRUCTURE
  /// and REDUNDANCY that real inputs of this domain have (repeated substrings,
  /// valid records/tokens, realistic value distributions) so the hot loop runs
  /// to completion over the whole input.
  ///
  /// The input MUST be a VALID input the operation processes end-to-end — one
  /// that is accepted, not rejected at a format/length/validation gate (a
  /// rejected input measures error handling, not the kernel). For an operation
  /// whose input is an ENCODED/COMPRESSED/PACKED blob (decode/decompress/
  /// verify/inverse), PRODUCE that blob by first running the FORWARD direction
  /// (the library's own encoder/compressor) over a large realistic buffer,
  /// then feed the result — do NOT hand a decoder raw or random bytes.
  ///
  /// Rules of thumb by category: text/format parsers → a large valid document
  /// with many records; codecs/compressors → a big buffer of realistic,
  /// compressible content; hashers → a big realistic data block; decoders →
  /// the encoder's output over such content; matrix/DP/search kernels → large
  /// dimensions / a long realistic haystack. Deterministic bytes. Operations
  /// whose work does NOT scale with input (config/option/getter/free ops)
  /// SHOULD be omitted — functional-only, not perf targets. Return one line
  /// per file written: `perf <op> <path>`.
  pub fn gen_perf(dir: &str) -> Vec<String>

Each runner fn takes (input_bytes, iters) and RETURNS the digest line(s)
as a String (no trailing newline needed; the shell prints it).

Hard rules:
  1. DETERMINISM: identical (input, iters) → identical returned String.
     Never include pointers/addresses, time, PIDs, paths, or HashMap
     iteration order. Floating-point values must be folded into an
     integer checksum (e.g. to_bits()), never formatted as decimals.
     CRITICAL — a raw pointer VALUE is an address even when masked:
     NEVER `fold(digest, some_ptr as u64)` or `as usize & 0xFF`. A
     function returning a `*mut`/`*const` (e.g. lodepng_chunk_next) gives
     an address — fold a CONTENT-derived fact instead: whether it is null
     (`p.is_null() as u64`), or its OFFSET from a known base
     (`(p as usize).wrapping_sub(base as usize) as u64`). An address low
     byte looks stable within one build but changes across builds/hosts,
     silently rotting the golden oracle.
  2. INPUT-SENSITIVITY: the digest MUST depend on the input bytes
     (<op>.1.bin and <op>.2.bin must yield different digests).
  3. ERRORS ARE DATA — NEVER EXIT OR PANIC: these runners are also used
     as fuzz targets fed with arbitrary malformed bytes. When the
     library reports an error, fold the error code into the digest
     (e.g. return "op=decode err=83 digest=0") and return normally.
     No std::process::exit, no panics/unwrap on input-dependent values,
     no slice indexing that can go out of bounds on short inputs.
  4. ITERS: when iters > 1, re-run the operation each iteration and fold
     each iteration's digest into a running wrapping checksum; return
     the digest once at the end. Iterations must not accumulate state
     that changes results (re-init library state each iteration).
  5. The heavy lifting must happen INSIDE the library-under-test; the
     harness only feeds inputs and folds outputs (checksum over output
     buffers, counts, sizes). Do not re-implement library logic.
  6. Free / clean up library-allocated buffers with the library's own
     free functions where provided (also on error paths — no leaks per
     iteration, fuzzing runs millions of executions).
  7. Runner fns registered in ops() must be safe `fn` items (wrap the
     unsafe FFI work inside the function body).
  8. PER-MODULE DUPLICATE TYPES (c2rust gotcha): c2rust emits the SAME C
     struct as a DISTINCT Rust type in EVERY module that references it —
     e.g. `json_tokener::json_object`, `json_patch::json_object` and
     `json_object::json_object` are three different types with IDENTICAL
     layout. The compiler will NOT unify them: passing a pointer returned by
     one module's fn into another module's fn is an E0308 `mismatched types`
     (`expected *mut a::T, found *mut b::T`). To bridge, CAST THE RAW POINTER
     at the call boundary: `foo_from_mod_b(p as *mut _)` (or
     `p as *const _` / `p.cast()`). Pick ONE module's type as canonical per
     struct and cast every cross-module pointer to it. Never assume two
     same-named structs from different modules are the same type, and never
     transmute whole values — cast the pointer.


Extend the harness to raise coverage: widen existing operations (extra
API calls on the same input/state, richer seed content that reaches more
branches, encoder options that trigger the unreached internal paths above)
and/or ADD new operations. If you add or rename operations you MUST also
output the updated spec.

Output format (BOTH blocks are mandatory):
1. ONE ```json block with the FULL updated spec (same schema as before,
   listing EVERY operation the file implements);
2. then ONE ```rust block with the complete updated src/lib.rs.

----- OUTPUT -----
```rust
use std::ffi::{c_char, c_void, CStr, CString};
use std::fs;
use std::mem::MaybeUninit;
use std::ptr;
use std::slice;

use miniz_raw::src::miniz as mz;
use miniz_raw::src::miniz_tdef as tdef;
use miniz_raw::src::miniz_tinfl as tinfl;
use miniz_raw::src::miniz_zip as zip;

fn fold(acc: u64, x: u64) -> u64 {
    acc.rotate_left(7) ^ x.wrapping_mul(0x9E37_79B1_85EB_CA87)
}

fn bytes_checksum(data: &[u8]) -> u64 {
    let mut acc = 0u64;
    for (i, &b) in data.iter().enumerate() {
        acc = fold(acc, ((i as u64) << 8) ^ b as u64);
    }
    acc
}

fn cstr_len(p: *const c_char) -> u64 {
    if p.is_null() {
        0
    } else {
        unsafe { CStr::from_ptr(p).to_bytes().len() as u64 }
    }
}

fn write_file(path: &str, bytes: &[u8]) -> bool {
    fs::write(path, bytes).is_ok()
}

fn make_text_payload(mult: usize) -> Vec<u8> {
    let mut out = Vec::with_capacity(mult * 256);
    for i in 0..mult {
        let level = match i % 5 {
            0 => "INFO",
            1 => "WARN",
            2 => "DEBUG",
            3 => "TRACE",
            _ => "ERROR",
        };
        let region = match i % 4 {
            0 => "us-east-1",
            1 => "eu-west-1",
            2 => "ap-south-1",
            _ => "local",
        };
        let line = format!(
            "{{\"ts\":\"2024-05-{day:02}T12:{min:02}:{sec:02}Z\",\"lvl\":\"{lvl}\",\"svc\":\"gateway\",\"region\":\"{region}\",\"req\":{req},\"user\":\"user_{user:05}\",\"path\":\"/api/v1/items/{item}\",\"status\":{status},\"latency_ms\":{lat},\"csv\":\"{a},{b},{c}\",\"msg\":\"deterministic repeated record block {blk}\"}}\n",
            day = (i % 28) + 1,
            min = i % 60,
            sec = (i * 7) % 60,
            lvl = level,
            region = region,
            req = 10_000u64 + i as u64,
            user = (i * 17) % 100_000,
            item = i % 4096,
            status = [200, 200, 200, 201, 404, 500][i % 6],
            lat = 3 + (i * 13) % 250,
            a = i,
            b = i.wrapping_mul(7),
            c = i ^ 0x55AA,
            blk = i % 128
        );
        out.extend_from_slice(line.as_bytes());
    }
    out
}

fn make_mixed_payload(mult: usize) -> Vec<u8> {
    let mut out = Vec::with_capacity(mult * 320);
    let header = b"MZRAW\x00HDR\x01\x02\x03\x04REPEAT-BLOCK:";
    for i in 0..mult {
        out.extend_from_slice(header);
        out.extend_from_slice(&(i as u32).to_le_bytes());
        out.extend_from_slice(&((i as u32).wrapping_mul(2654435761)).to_le_bytes());
        let text = format!(
            "section={},name=file_{:06}.bin,type=chunk,flags={:04x},note=structured-binary-looking-data\n",
            i,
            i,
            (i * 9) & 0xFFFF
        );
        out.extend_from_slice(text.as_bytes());
        for j in 0..48usize {
            let v = (((i as u32).wrapping_mul(31)).wrapping_add(j as u32 * 17) ^ 0xA5A55A5A)
                .to_le_bytes();
            out.extend_from_slice(&v);
        }
        out.extend_from_slice(b"\n--PAYLOAD-SPLIT--\n");
        out.extend_from_slice(
            b"HTTP/1.1 200 OK\r\nContent-Type: application/octet-stream\r\nX-Repeat: yes\r\n\r\n",
        );
    }
    out
}

fn make_perf_payload() -> Vec<u8> {
    let mut out = Vec::new();
    out.extend_from_slice(&make_text_payload(28_000));
    out.extend_from_slice(&make_mixed_payload(18_000));
    out
}

unsafe extern "C" fn zip_write_cb(
    opaque: *mut c_void,
    file_ofs: zip::mz_uint64,
    p_buf: *const c_void,
    n: usize,
) -> usize {
    let st = &mut *(opaque as *mut ZipCbState);
    st.calls = st.calls.wrapping_add(1);
    st.total = st.total.wrapping_add(n as u64);
    st.digest = fold(st.digest, file_ofs);
    if !p_buf.is_null() && n != 0 {
        let bytes = slice::from_raw_parts(p_buf as *const u8, n);
        st.digest = fold(st.digest, bytes_checksum(bytes));
    }
    n
}

unsafe extern "C" fn tinfl_put_cb(p_buf: *const c_void, len: i32, user: *mut c_void) -> i32 {
    let st = &mut *(user as *mut TinflCbState);
    let n = if len < 0 { 0usize } else { len as usize };
    st.calls = st.calls.wrapping_add(1);
    st.total = st.total.wrapping_add(n as u64);
    if !p_buf.is_null() && n != 0 {
        let bytes = slice::from_raw_parts(p_buf as *const u8, n);
        st.buf.extend_from_slice(bytes);
        st.digest = fold(st.digest, bytes_checksum(bytes));
    }
    1
}

unsafe extern "C" fn tdefl_put_cb(p_buf: *const c_void, len: i32, user: *mut c_void) -> i32 {
    let st = &mut *(user as *mut TdeflCbState);
    let n = if len < 0 { 0usize } else { len as usize };
    st.calls = st.calls.wrapping_add(1);
    st.total = st.total.wrapping_add(n as u64);
    if !p_buf.is_null() && n != 0 {
        let bytes = slice::from_raw_parts(p_buf as *const u8, n);
        st.buf.extend_from_slice(bytes);
        st.digest = fold(st.digest, bytes_checksum(bytes));
    }
    1
}

unsafe extern "C" fn read_buf_cb(
    opaque: *mut c_void,
    file_ofs: zip::mz_uint64,
    p_buf: *mut c_void,
    n: usize,
) -> usize {
    let st = &mut *(opaque as *mut ReadBufState);
    let start = (file_ofs as usize).min(st.data.len());
    let end = start.saturating_add(n).min(st.data.len());
    let amt = end.saturating_sub(start);
    st.calls = st.calls.wrapping_add(1);
    st.total = st.total.wrapping_add(amt as u64);
    st.digest = fold(st.digest, file_ofs);
    if amt != 0 && !p_buf.is_null() {
        ptr::copy_nonoverlapping(st.data[start..end].as_ptr(), p_buf as *mut u8, amt);
        st.digest = fold(st.digest, bytes_checksum(&st.data[start..end]));
    }
    amt
}

#[derive(Default)]
struct ZipCbState {
    total: u64,
    calls: u64,
    digest: u64,
}

#[derive(Default)]
struct TinflCbState {
    total: u64,
    calls: u64,
    digest: u64,
    buf: Vec<u8>,
}

#[derive(Default)]
struct TdeflCbState {
    total: u64,
    calls: u64,
    digest: u64,
    buf: Vec<u8>,
}

struct ReadBufState<'a> {
    data: &'a [u8],
    total: u64,
    calls: u64,
    digest: u64,
}

fn compress_zlib_blob(data: &[u8], level: i32) -> Option<Vec<u8>> {
    unsafe {
        let bound = mz::mz_compressBound(data.len() as mz::mz_ulong) as usize;
        let mut out = vec![0u8; bound.max(1)];
        let mut out_len = out.len() as mz::mz_ulong;
        let rc = mz::mz_compress2(
            out.as_mut_ptr(),
            &mut out_len,
            if data.is_empty() { ptr::null() } else { data.as_ptr() },
            data.len() as mz::mz_ulong,
            level,
        );
        if rc >= 0 {
            out.truncate(out_len as usize);
            Some(out)
        } else {
            None
        }
    }
}

fn build_zip_blob(members: &[(&[u8], &'static [u8], Option<&'static [u8]>)]) -> Option<Vec<u8>> {
    unsafe {
        let mut za = MaybeUninit::<zip::mz_zip_archive>::zeroed();
        let pzip = za.as_mut_ptr();
        zip::mz_zip_zero_struct(pzip);

        if zip::mz_zip_writer_init_heap(pzip, 0, 0) == 0 {
            let _ = zip::mz_zip_writer_end(pzip);
            return None;
        }

        let mut ok = true;
        for (data, name, comment) in members.iter() {
            let added = if let Some(c) = comment {
                zip::mz_zip_writer_add_mem_ex(
                    pzip,
                    name.as_ptr() as *const c_char,
                    if data.is_empty() {
                        ptr::null()
                    } else {
                        data.as_ptr() as *const c_void
                    },
                    data.len(),
                    c.as_ptr() as *const c_void,
                    c.len() as u16,
                    6u32,
                    0,
                    0,
                )
            } else {
                zip::mz_zip_writer_add_mem(
                    pzip,
                    name.as_ptr() as *const c_char,
                    if data.is_empty() {
                        ptr::null()
                    } else {
                        data.as_ptr() as *const c_void
                    },
                    data.len(),
                    6u32,
                )
            };
            if added == 0 {
                ok = false;
                break;
            }
        }

        let mut heap_ptr: *mut c_void = ptr::null_mut();
        let mut heap_size: usize = 0;
        if ok {
            ok = zip::mz_zip_writer_finalize_heap_archive(pzip, &mut heap_ptr, &mut heap_size) != 0;
        }

        let out = if ok && !heap_ptr.is_null() {
            let bytes = slice::from_raw_parts(heap_ptr as *const u8, heap_size).to_vec();
            mz::mz_free(heap_ptr);
            Some(bytes)
        } else {
            if !heap_ptr.is_null() {
                mz::mz_free(heap_ptr);
            }
            None
        };

        let _ = zip::mz_zip_writer_end(pzip);
        out
    }
}

fn mz_stream_roundtrip(input: &[u8], iters: u64) -> String {
    let mut digest = 0u64;
    let mut last_def_rc = 0i32;
    let mut last_inf_rc = 0i32;
    let mut last_err_strlen = 0u64;

    for _ in 0..iters {
        unsafe {
            digest = fold(digest, cstr_len(mz::mz_version()));

            let mut def = MaybeUninit::<mz::mz_stream>::zeroed().assume_init();
            let mut comp: Vec<u8> = Vec::new();
            let mut recovered: Vec<u8> = Vec::new();

            let init_rc = mz::mz_deflateInit2(&mut def as *mut _, 6, 8, 15, 9, 0);
            last_def_rc = init_rc;
            digest = fold(digest, init_rc as u64);
            if init_rc == 0 {
                let _ = mz::mz_deflateReset(&mut def as *mut _);
                let bound =
                    mz::mz_deflateBound(&mut def as *mut _, input.len() as mz::mz_ulong) as usize;
                let cap = bound.max(128);
                comp.resize(cap, 0u8);

                let mut in_pos = 0usize;
                loop {
                    if def.avail_in == 0 && in_pos < input.len() {
                        let chunk = (input.len() - in_pos).min(1024);
                        def.next_in = input[in_pos..].as_ptr();
                        def.avail_in = chunk as u32;
                        in_pos += chunk;
                    }
                    if def.avail_out == 0 {
                        let out_pos = def.total_out as usize;
                        if out_pos >= comp.len() {
                            comp.resize(comp.len().saturating_add(1024).max(1024), 0);
                        }
                        def.next_out = comp[out_pos..].as_mut_ptr();
                        def.avail_out = (comp.len() - out_pos) as u32;
                    }

                    let flush = if in_pos >= input.len() && def.avail_in == 0 { 4 } else { 0 };
                    let rc = mz::mz_deflate(&mut def as *mut _, flush);
                    last_def_rc = rc;
                    digest = fold(digest, rc as u64);
                    if rc == 1 || rc < 0 {
                        break;
                    }
                    if flush == 4 && def.avail_out != 0 && rc == 0 && def.avail_in == 0 {
                        break;
                    }
                }

                comp.truncate(def.total_out as usize);
                let _ = mz::mz_deflateEnd(&mut def as *mut _);
            }

            let mut inf = MaybeUninit::<mz::mz_stream>::zeroed().assume_init();
            let inf_init = mz::mz_inflateInit2(&mut inf as *mut _, 15);
            last_inf_rc = inf_init;
            digest = fold(digest, inf_init as u64);
            if inf_init == 0 {
                let _ = mz::mz_inflateReset(&mut inf as *mut _);
                recovered.resize(input.len().saturating_add(1024).max(128), 0u8);

                let mut in_pos = 0usize;
                loop {
                    if inf.avail_in == 0 && in_pos < comp.len() {
                        let chunk = (comp.len() - in_pos).min(777);
                        inf.next_in = comp[in_pos..].as_ptr();
                        inf.avail_in = chunk as u32;
                        in_pos += chunk;
                    }
                    if inf.avail_out == 0 {
                        let out_pos = inf.total_out as usize;
                        if out_pos >= recovered.len() {
                            recovered.resize(recovered.len().saturating_add(1024).max(1024), 0);
                        }
                        inf.next_out = recovered[out_pos..].as_mut_ptr();
                        inf.avail_out = (recovered.len() - out_pos) as u32;
                    }

                    let rc = mz::mz_inflate(&mut inf as *mut _, 0);
                    last_inf_rc = rc;
                    digest = fold(digest, rc as u64);
                    if rc == 1 || rc < 0 {
                        break;
                    }
                    if in_pos >= comp.len() && inf.avail_in == 0 && rc == 0 && inf.avail_out != 0 {
                        break;
                    }
                }

                recovered.truncate(inf.total_out as usize);
                let _ = mz::mz_inflateEnd(&mut inf as *mut _);
            }

            let in_adler = mz::mz_adler32(
                1,
                if input.is_empty() { ptr::null() } else { input.as_ptr() },
                input.len(),
            );
            let in_crc = mz::mz_crc32(
                0,
                if input.is_empty() { ptr::null() } else { input.as_ptr() },
                input.len(),
            );
            let out_adler = mz::mz_adler32(
                1,
                if recovered.is_empty() {
                    ptr::null()
                } else {
                    recovered.as_ptr()
                },
                recovered.len(),
            );
            let out_crc = mz::mz_crc32(
                0,
                if recovered.is_empty() {
                    ptr::null()
                } else {
                    recovered.as_ptr()
                },
                recovered.len(),
            );

            let mut one_shot = vec![0u8; mz::mz_compressBound(input.len() as mz::mz_ulong) as usize + 1];
            let mut one_shot_len = one_shot.len() as mz::mz_ulong;
            let c1 = mz::mz_compress(
                one_shot.as_mut_ptr(),
                &mut one_shot_len,
                if input.is_empty() { ptr::null() } else { input.as_ptr() },
                input.len() as mz::mz_ulong,
            );
            digest = fold(digest, c1 as u64);
            if c1 >= 0 {
                one_shot.truncate(one_shot_len as usize);
                let mut dec = vec![0u8; input.len().saturating_add(64).max(1)];
                let mut dec_len = dec.len() as mz::mz_ulong;
                let u1 = mz::mz_uncompress(
                    dec.as_mut_ptr(),
                    &mut dec_len,
                    if one_shot.is_empty() {
                        ptr::null()
                    } else {
                        one_shot.as_ptr()
                    },
                    one_shot.len() as mz::mz_ulong,
                );
                digest = fold(digest, u1 as u64);
                if u1 >= 0 {
                    dec.truncate(dec_len as usize);
                    digest = fold(digest, bytes_checksum(&dec));
                    digest = fold(digest, (dec == input) as u64);
                }

                let mut dec2 = vec![0u8; input.len().saturating_add(64).max(1)];
                let mut dec2_len = dec2.len() as mz::mz_ulong;
                let mut src_len = one_shot.len() as mz::mz_ulong;
                let u2 = mz::mz_uncompress2(
                    dec2.as_mut_ptr(),
                    &mut dec2_len,
                    if one_shot.is_empty() {
                        ptr::null()
                    } else {
                        one_shot.as_ptr()
                    },
                    &mut src_len,
                );
                digest = fold(digest, u2 as u64);
                digest = fold(digest, src_len as u64);
                if u2 >= 0 {
                    dec2.truncate(dec2_len as usize);
                    digest = fold(digest, bytes_checksum(&dec2));
                    digest = fold(digest, (dec2 == input) as u64);
                }
            }

            last_err_strlen = cstr_len(mz::mz_error(last_inf_rc));
            digest = fold(digest, input.len() as u64);
            digest = fold(digest, comp.len() as u64);
            digest = fold(digest, recovered.len() as u64);
            digest = fold(digest, in_adler as u64);
            digest = fold(digest, in_crc as u64);
            digest = fold(digest, out_adler as u64);
            digest = fold(digest, out_crc as u64);
            digest = fold(digest, bytes_checksum(&recovered));
            digest = fold(digest, (input == recovered) as u64);
            digest = fold(digest, last_err_strlen);
        }
    }

    format!(
        "op=mz_stream_roundtrip def_rc={} inf_rc={} errlen={} digest={:016x}",
        last_def_rc, last_inf_rc, last_err_strlen, digest
    )
}

fn tinfl_decode_blob(input: &[u8], iters: u64) -> String {
    let mut digest = 0u64;
    let mut last_cb_rc = 0i32;

    for _ in 0..iters {
        unsafe {
            let mut out_len_heap: usize = 0;
            let heap_ptr = tinfl::tinfl_decompress_mem_to_heap(
                if input.is_empty() {
                    ptr::null()
                } else {
                    input.as_ptr() as *const c_void
                },
                input.len(),
                &mut out_len_heap,
                1,
            );

            let mut heap_bytes: &[u8] = &[];
            if !heap_ptr.is_null() && out_len_heap != 0 {
                heap_bytes = slice::from_raw_parts(heap_ptr as *const u8, out_len_heap);
            }

            let cap_guess = if !heap_bytes.is_empty() {
                heap_bytes.len()
            } else {
                input
                    .len()
                    .saturating_mul(64)
                    .saturating_add(4096)
                    .min(64 * 1024 * 1024)
                    .max(1)
            };
            let mut mem_buf = vec![0u8; cap_guess];
            let mem_out = tinfl::tinfl_decompress_mem_to_mem(
                mem_buf.as_mut_ptr() as *mut c_void,
                mem_buf.len(),
                if input.is_empty() {
                    ptr::null()
                } else {
                    input.as_ptr() as *const c_void
                },
                input.len(),
                1,
            );

            let mem_ok = mem_out != usize::MAX && mem_out <= mem_buf.len();
            if mem_ok {
                mem_buf.truncate(mem_out);
            } else {
                mem_buf.clear();
            }

            let mut cb_in_size = input.len();
            let mut cb_state = TinflCbState::default();
            last_cb_rc = tinfl::tinfl_decompress_mem_to_callback(
                if input.is_empty() {
                    ptr::null()
                } else {
                    input.as_ptr() as *const c_void
                },
                &mut cb_in_size,
                Some(tinfl_put_cb),
                &mut cb_state as *mut _ as *mut c_void,
                1,
            );

            let decomp = tinfl::tinfl_decompressor_alloc();
            digest = fold(digest, decomp.is_null() as u64);
            if !decomp.is_null() {
                let mut in_size = input.len();
                let mut out = vec![0u8; heap_bytes.len().max(mem_buf.len()).max(4096)];
                let mut out_size = out.len();
                let status = tinfl::tinfl_decompress(
                    decomp,
                    if input.is_empty() { ptr::null() } else { input.as_ptr() },
                    &mut in_size,
                    out.as_mut_ptr(),
                    out.as_mut_ptr(),
                    &mut out_size,
                    1,
                );
                digest = fold(digest, status as u64);
                digest = fold(digest, in_size as u64);
                digest = fold(digest, out_size as u64);
                if out_size <= out.len() {
                    digest = fold(digest, bytes_checksum(&out[..out_size]));
                }
                tinfl::tinfl_decompressor_free(decomp);
            }

            let heap_crc = mz::mz_crc32(
                0,
                if heap_bytes.is_empty() {
                    ptr::null()
                } else {
                    heap_bytes.as_ptr()
                },
                heap_bytes.len(),
            );
            let heap_adler = mz::mz_adler32(
                1,
                if heap_bytes.is_empty() {
                    ptr::null()
                } else {
                    heap_bytes.as_ptr()
                },
                heap_bytes.len(),
            );
            let mem_crc = mz::mz_crc32(
                0,
                if mem_buf.is_empty() {
                    ptr::null()
                } else {
                    mem_buf.as_ptr()
                },
                mem_buf.len(),
            );
            let mem_adler = mz::mz_adler32(
                1,
                if mem_buf.is_empty() {
                    ptr::null()
                } else {
                    mem_buf.as_ptr()
                },
                mem_buf.len(),
            );
            let cb_crc = mz::mz_crc32(
                0,
                if cb_state.buf.is_empty() {
                    ptr::null()
                } else {
                    cb_state.buf.as_ptr()
                },
                cb_state.buf.len(),
            );
            let cb_adler = mz::mz_adler32(
                1,
                if cb_state.buf.is_empty() {
                    ptr::null()
                } else {
                    cb_state.buf.as_ptr()
                },
                cb_state.buf.len(),
            );

            digest = fold(digest, input.len() as u64);
            digest = fold(digest, cb_in_size as u64);
            digest = fold(digest, out_len_heap as u64);
            digest = fold(digest, mem_out as u64);
            digest = fold(digest, last_cb_rc as u64);
            digest = fold(digest, heap_crc as u64);
            digest = fold(digest, heap_adler as u64);
            digest = fold(digest, mem_crc as u64);
            digest = fold(digest, mem_adler as u64);
            digest = fold(digest, cb_crc as u64);
            digest = fold(digest, cb_adler as u64);
            digest = fold(digest, cb_state.total);
            digest = fold(digest, cb_state.calls);
            digest = fold(digest, cb_state.digest);
            digest = fold(digest, (heap_bytes == mem_buf.as_slice()) as u64);
            digest = fold(digest, (heap_bytes == cb_state.buf.as_slice()) as u64);
            digest = fold(digest, bytes_checksum(heap_bytes));
            digest = fold(digest, bytes_checksum(&mem_buf));
            digest = fold(digest, bytes_checksum(&cb_state.buf));

            if !heap_ptr.is_null() {
                mz::mz_free(heap_ptr);
            }
        }
    }

    format!("op=tinfl_decode_blob cb_rc={} digest={:016x}", last_cb_rc, digest)
}

fn tdefl_encode_blob(input: &[u8], iters: u64) -> String {
    let mut digest = 0u64;
    let mut last_status = 0i32;

    for _ in 0..iters {
        unsafe {
            let flags = tdef::tdefl_create_comp_flags_from_zip_params(6, 15, 0) as i32;

            let comp = tdef::tdefl_compressor_alloc();
            digest = fold(digest, comp.is_null() as u64);
            if !comp.is_null() {
                let mut cb = TdeflCbState::default();
                let init_st = tdef::tdefl_init(comp, Some(tdefl_put_cb), &mut cb as *mut _ as *mut c_void, flags);
                digest = fold(digest, init_st as u64);

                let mut in_sz = input.len();
                let mut out_buf = vec![0u8; mz::mz_compressBound(input.len() as mz::mz_ulong) as usize + 64];
                let mut out_sz = out_buf.len();
                let st = tdef::tdefl_compress(
                    comp,
                    if input.is_empty() { ptr::null() } else { input.as_ptr() as *const c_void },
                    &mut in_sz,
                    out_buf.as_mut_ptr() as *mut c_void,
                    &mut out_sz,
                    4,
                );
                last_status = st as i32;
                digest = fold(digest, st as u64);
                digest = fold(digest, in_sz as u64);
                digest = fold(digest, out_sz as u64);
                if out_sz <= out_buf.len() {
                    digest = fold(digest, bytes_checksum(&out_buf[..out_sz]));
                }

                let prev = tdef::tdefl_get_prev_return_status(comp);
                let ad = tdef::tdefl_get_adler32(comp);
                digest = fold(digest, prev as u64);
                digest = fold(digest, ad as u64);
                digest = fold(digest, cb.total);
                digest = fold(digest, cb.calls);
                digest = fold(digest, cb.digest);
                digest = fold(digest, bytes_checksum(&cb.buf));

                tdef::tdefl_compressor_free(comp);
            }

            let mut heap_len = 0usize;
            let heap_ptr = tdef::tdefl_compress_mem_to_heap(
                if input.is_empty() { ptr::null() } else { input.as_ptr() as *const c_void },
                input.len(),
                &mut heap_len,
                flags,
            );
            digest = fold(digest, heap_len as u64);
            if !heap_ptr.is_null() {
                let heap = slice::from_raw_parts(heap_ptr as *const u8, heap_len);
                digest = fold(digest, bytes_checksum(heap));
                mz::mz_free(heap_ptr);
            }

            let mut mem = vec![0u8; mz::mz_compressBound(input.len() as mz::mz_ulong) as usize + 64];
            let mem_len = tdef::tdefl_compress_mem_to_mem(
                mem.as_mut_ptr() as *mut c_void,
                mem.len(),
                if input.is_empty() { ptr::null() } else { input.as_ptr() as *const c_void },
                input.len(),
                flags,
            );
            digest = fold(digest, mem_len as u64);
            if mem_len != usize::MAX && mem_len <= mem.len() {
                digest = fold(digest, bytes_checksum(&mem[..mem_len]));
            }

            let mut cb2 = TdeflCbState::default();
            let ok = tdef::tdefl_compress_mem_to_output(
                if input.is_empty() { ptr::null() } else { input.as_ptr() as *const c_void },
                input.len(),
                Some(tdefl_put_cb),
                &mut cb2 as *mut _ as *mut c_void,
                flags,
            );
            digest = fold(digest, ok as u64);
            digest = fold(digest, cb2.total);
            digest = fold(digest, cb2.calls);
            digest = fold(digest, cb2.digest);
            digest = fold(digest, bytes_checksum(&cb2.buf));

            let w = 16i32;
            let h = ((input.len() / 64).max(1).min(64)) as i32;
            let need = (w as usize) * (h as usize) * 4;
            let mut img = vec![0u8; need];
            for i in 0..need {
                img[i] = input.get(i % input.len().max(1)).copied().unwrap_or(0).wrapping_add(i as u8);
            }

            let mut png_len1 = 0usize;
            let png1 = tdef::tdefl_write_image_to_png_file_in_memory(
                img.as_ptr() as *const c_void,
                w,
                h,
                4,
                &mut png_len1,
            );
            digest = fold(digest, png_len1 as u64);
            if !png1.is_null() {
                let png = slice::from_raw_parts(png1 as *const u8, png_len1);
                digest = fold(digest, bytes_checksum(png));
                mz::mz_free(png1);
            }

            let mut png_len2 = 0usize;
            let png2 = tdef::tdefl_write_image_to_png_file_in_memory_ex(
                img.as_ptr() as *const c_void,
                w,
                h,
                4,
                &mut png_len2,
                6,
                1,
            );
            digest = fold(digest, png_len2 as u64);
            if !png2.is_null() {
                let png = slice::from_raw_parts(png2 as *const u8, png_len2);
                digest = fold(digest, bytes_checksum(png));
                mz::mz_free(png2);
            }
        }
    }

    format!("op=tdefl_encode_blob status={} digest={:016x}", last_status, digest)
}

fn zip_mem_roundtrip(input: &[u8], iters: u64) -> String {
    let mut digest = 0u64;
    let mut last_files = 0u64;
    let name1 = b"payload.bin\0";
    let name2 = b"mirror.dat\0";
    let comment2 = b"member-comment";

    for _ in 0..iters {
        let mut mirrored = Vec::with_capacity(input.len().saturating_add(16));
        mirrored.extend_from_slice(input);
        mirrored.extend_from_slice(b"::mirror::");
        mirrored.extend(input.iter().rev().take(input.len().min(128)));

        let members = [
            (input, name1.as_slice(), None),
            (mirrored.as_slice(), name2.as_slice(), Some(comment2.as_slice())),
        ];

        let archive = match build_zip_blob(&members) {
            Some(v) => v,
            None => {
                digest = fold(digest, 0);
                continue;
            }
        };

        unsafe {
            let mut za = MaybeUninit::<zip::mz_zip_archive>::zeroed();
            let pzip = za.as_mut_ptr();
            zip::mz_zip_zero_struct(pzip);

            let init_ok = zip::mz_zip_reader_init_mem(
                pzip,
                archive.as_ptr() as *const c_void,
                archive.len(),
                0,
            );
            digest = fold(digest, init_ok as u64);

            if init_ok != 0 {
                digest = fold(digest, zip::mz_zip_get_mode(pzip) as u64);
                digest = fold(digest, zip::mz_zip_get_type(pzip) as u64);
                digest = fold(digest, zip::mz_zip_get_archive_file_start_offset(pzip));
                digest = fold(digest, zip::mz_zip_get_cfile(pzip).is_null() as u64);

                let num_files = zip::mz_zip_reader_get_num_files(pzip) as u64;
                last_files = num_files;
                digest = fold(digest, num_files);

                let loc1 = zip::mz_zip_reader_locate_file(
                    pzip,
                    name1.as_ptr() as *const c_char,
                    ptr::null(),
                    0,
                );
                let mut idx2: u32 = 0;
                let loc2 = zip::mz_zip_reader_locate_file_v2(
                    pzip,
                    name2.as_ptr() as *const c_char,
                    ptr::null(),
                    0,
                    &mut idx2,
                );
                digest = fold(digest, loc1 as u64);
                digest = fold(digest, idx2 as u64);
                digest = fold(digest, loc2 as u64);

                let sup1 = if loc1 >= 0 {
                    zip::mz_zip_reader_is_file_supported(pzip, loc1 as u32)
                } else {
                    0
                };
                let dir1 = if loc1 >= 0 {
                    zip::mz_zip_reader_is_file_a_directory(pzip, loc1 as u32)
                } else {
                    0
                };
                digest = fold(digest, sup1 as u64);
                digest = fold(digest, dir1 as u64);

                let mut fname = vec![0i8; 256];
                let fname_len = if loc1 >= 0 {
                    zip::mz_zip_reader_get_filename(
                        pzip,
                        loc1 as u32,
                        fname.as_mut_ptr(),
                        fname.len() as u32,
                    )
                } else {
                    0
                };
                digest = fold(digest, fname_len as u64);

                let mut stat = MaybeUninit::<zip::mz_zip_archive_file_stat>::zeroed();
                let stat_ok = if loc1 >= 0 {
                    zip::mz_zip_reader_file_stat(pzip, loc1 as u32, stat.as_mut_ptr())
                } else {
                    0
                };
                digest = fold(digest, stat_ok as u64);

                let valid = zip::mz_zip_validate_archive(pzip, 0);
                digest = fold(digest, valid as u64);

                let mut hdr = vec![0u8; archive.len().min(64).max(1)];
                let rd = zip::mz_zip_read_archive_data(
                    pzip,
                    0,
                    hdr.as_mut_ptr() as *mut c_void,
                    hdr.len(),
                );
                digest = fold(digest, rd as u64);
                digest = fold(digest, bytes_checksum(&hdr[..rd.min(hdr.len())]));

                let mut out1 = vec![0u8; input.len().max(1)];
                let ex1 = if loc1 >= 0 {
                    zip::mz_zip_reader_extract_to_mem(
                        pzip,
                        loc1 as u32,
                        out1.as_mut_ptr() as *mut c_void,
                        out1.len(),
                        0,
                    )
                } else {
                    0
                };
                digest = fold(digest, ex1 as u64);
                if ex1 != 0 {
                    let crc1 = mz::mz_crc32(0, out1.as_ptr(), out1.len());
                    let ad1 = mz::mz_adler32(1, out1.as_ptr(), out1.len());
                    digest = fold(digest, crc1 as u64);
                    digest = fold(digest, ad1 as u64);
                    digest = fold(digest, bytes_checksum(&out1));
                }

                let mut out2_len: usize = 0;
                let out2_ptr = if loc2 != 0 {
                    zip::mz_zip_reader_extract_to_heap(pzip, idx2, &mut out2_len, 0)
                } else {
                    ptr::null_mut()
                };
                digest = fold(digest, out2_len as u64);
                if !out2_ptr.is_null() {
                    let out2 = slice::from_raw_parts(out2_ptr as *const u8, out2_len);
                    let crc2 = mz::mz_crc32(
                        0,
                        if out2.is_empty() { ptr::null() } else { out2.as_ptr() },
                        out2.len(),
                    );
                    let ad2 = mz::mz_adler32(
                        1,
                        if out2.is_empty() { ptr::null() } else { out2.as_ptr() },
                        out2.len(),
                    );
                    digest = fold(digest, crc2 as u64);
                    digest = fold(digest, ad2 as u64);
                    digest = fold(digest, bytes_checksum(out2));
                    mz::mz_free(out2_ptr);
                }

                let mut cb = ZipCbState::default();
                let ex_cb = if loc1 >= 0 {
                    zip::mz_zip_reader_extract_to_callback(
                        pzip,
                        loc1 as u32,
                        Some(zip_write_cb),
                        &mut cb as *mut _ as *mut c_void,
                        0,
                    )
                } else {
                    0
                };
                digest = fold(digest, ex_cb as u64);
                digest = fold(digest, cb.total);
                digest = fold(digest, cb.calls);
                digest = fold(digest, cb.digest);

                let _ = zip::mz_zip_reader_end(pzip);
                let _ = zip::mz_zip_end(pzip);
            } else {
                let _ = zip::mz_zip_end(pzip);
            }

            digest = fold(digest, archive.len() as u64);
            digest = fold(digest, mz::mz_crc32(0, archive.as_ptr(), archive.len()) as u64);
        }
    }

    format!("op=zip_mem_roundtrip files={} digest={:016x}", last_files, digest)
}

fn zip_reader_blob(input: &[u8], iters: u64) -> String {
    let mut digest = 0u64;
    let mut last_err_code = 0u64;

    let alpha = b"alpha.txt\0";
    let beta = b"beta.bin\0";
    let gamma = b"gamma/log.json\0";

    for _ in 0..iters {
        unsafe {
            let mut mem_err: zip::mz_zip_error = 0;
            let valid_mem = zip::mz_zip_validate_mem_archive(
                if input.is_empty() {
                    ptr::null()
                } else {
                    input.as_ptr() as *const c_void
                },
                input.len(),
                0,
                &mut mem_err,
            );
            digest = fold(digest, valid_mem as u64);
            digest = fold(digest, mem_err as u64);

            let mut za = MaybeUninit::<zip::mz_zip_archive>::zeroed();
            let pzip = za.as_mut_ptr();
            zip::mz_zip_zero_struct(pzip);

            let init_ok = zip::mz_zip_reader_init_mem(
                pzip,
                if input.is_empty() {
                    ptr::null()
                } else {
                    input.as_ptr() as *const c_void
                },
                input.len(),
                0,
            );
            digest = fold(digest, init_ok as u64);

            if init_ok != 0 {
                digest = fold(digest, zip::mz_zip_get_mode(pzip) as u64);
                digest = fold(digest, zip::mz_zip_get_type(pzip) as u64);
                digest = fold(digest, zip::mz_zip_get_archive_file_start_offset(pzip));
                digest = fold(digest, zip::mz_zip_get_cfile(pzip).is_null() as u64);

                let valid = zip::mz_zip_validate_archive(pzip, 0);
                let num = zip::mz_zip_reader_get_num_files(pzip) as u64;
                let arch_sz = zip::mz_zip_get_archive_size(pzip);
                let cd_sz = zip::mz_zip_get_central_dir_size(pzip);
                let zip64 = zip::mz_zip_is_zip64(pzip);
                digest = fold(digest, valid as u64);
                digest = fold(digest, num);
                digest = fold(digest, arch_sz);
                digest = fold(digest, cd_sz as u64);
                digest = fold(digest, zip64 as u64);

                let mut hdr = vec![0u8; input.len().min(128).max(1)];
                let rd = zip::mz_zip_read_archive_data(
                    pzip,
                    0,
                    hdr.as_mut_ptr() as *mut c_void,
                    hdr.len(),
                );
                digest = fold(digest, rd as u64);
                digest = fold(digest, bytes_checksum(&hdr[..rd.min(hdr.len())]));

                let _ = zip::mz_zip_set_last_error(pzip, mem_err);
                digest = fold(digest, zip::mz_zip_peek_last_error(pzip) as u64);
                let _ = zip::mz_zip_clear_last_error(pzip);
                digest = fold(digest, zip::mz_zip_peek_last_error(pzip) as u64);

                for name in [alpha.as_slice(), beta.as_slice(), gamma.as_slice()] {
                    let loc = zip::mz_zip_reader_locate_file(
                        pzip,
                        name.as_ptr() as *const c_char,
                        ptr::null(),
                        0,
                    );
                    let mut idx: u32 = 0;
                    let loc2 = zip::mz_zip_reader_locate_file_v2(
                        pzip,
                        name.as_ptr() as *const c_char,
                        ptr::null(),
                        0,
                        &mut idx,
                    );
                    digest = fold(digest, loc as u64);
                    digest = fold(digest, idx as u64);
                    digest = fold(digest, loc2 as u64);

                    let found = loc >= 0 || loc2 != 0;
                    if !found {
                        continue;
                    }

                    let qidx = if loc >= 0 { loc as u32 } else { idx };
                    let enc = zip::mz_zip_reader_is_file_encrypted(pzip, qidx);
                    let sup = zip::mz_zip_reader_is_file_supported(pzip, qidx);
                    let dir = zip::mz_zip_reader_is_file_a_directory(pzip, qidx);
                    let vf = zip::mz_zip_validate_file(pzip, qidx, 0);
                    digest = fold(digest, enc as u64);
                    digest = fold(digest, sup as u64);
                    digest = fold(digest, dir as u64);
                    digest = fold(digest, vf as u64);

                    let mut fname = vec![0i8; 256];
                    let fnlen = zip::mz_zip_reader_get_filename(
                        pzip,
                        qidx,
                        fname.as_mut_ptr(),
                        fname.len() as u32,
                    );
                    digest = fold(digest, fnlen as u64);

                    let mut stat = MaybeUninit::<zip::mz_zip_archive_file_stat>::zeroed();
                    let stok = zip::mz_zip_reader_file_stat(pzip, qidx, stat.as_mut_ptr());
                    digest = fold(digest, stok as u64);

                    let buf_cap = input
                        .len()
                        .saturating_mul(16)
                        .saturating_add(4096)
                        .min(64 * 1024 * 1024)
                        .max(1);
                    let mut mem_buf = vec![0u8; buf_cap];
                    let exm = zip::mz_zip_reader_extract_to_mem(
                        pzip,
                        qidx,
                        mem_buf.as_mut_ptr() as *mut c_void,
                        mem_buf.len(),
                        0,
                    );
                    digest = fold(digest, exm as u64);
                    if exm != 0 {
                        let crc = mz::mz_crc32(0, mem_buf.as_ptr(), mem_buf.len());
                        digest = fold(digest, crc as u64);
                        digest = fold(digest, bytes_checksum(&mem_buf));
                    }

                    let mut heap_len: usize = 0;
                    let heap_ptr = zip::mz_zip_reader_extract_to_heap(pzip, qidx, &mut heap_len, 0);
                    digest = fold(digest, heap_len as u64);
                    if !heap_ptr.is_null() {
                        let heap = slice::from_raw_parts(heap_ptr as *const u8, heap_len);
                        let crc = mz::mz_crc32(
                            0,
                            if heap.is_empty() { ptr::null() } else { heap.as_ptr() },
                            heap.len(),
                        );
                        digest = fold(digest, crc as u64);
                        digest = fold(digest, bytes_checksum(heap));
                        mz::mz_free(heap_ptr);
                    }

                    let iter = zip::mz_zip_reader_extract_iter_new(pzip, qidx, 0);
                    digest = fold(digest, iter.is_null() as u64);
                    if !iter.is_null() {
                        let mut total_iter = 0u64;
                        let mut buf = vec![0u8; 1024];
                        loop {
                            let n = zip::mz_zip_reader_extract_iter_read(
                                iter,
                                buf.as_mut_ptr() as *mut c_void,
                                buf.len(),
                            );
                            if n == 0 {
                                break;
                            }
                            total_iter = total_iter.wrapping_add(n as u64);
                            digest = fold(digest, bytes_checksum(&buf[..n]));
                        }
                        digest = fold(digest, total_iter);
                        let fr = zip::mz_zip_reader_extract_iter_free(iter);
                        digest = fold(digest, fr as u64);
                    }

                    let iter2 = zip::mz_zip_reader_extract_file_iter_new(
                        pzip,
                        name.as_ptr() as *const c_char,
                        0,
                    );
                    digest = fold(digest, iter2.is_null() as u64);
                    if !iter2.is_null() {
                        let mut total_iter = 0u64;
                        let mut buf = vec![0u8; 333];
                        loop {
                            let n = zip::mz_zip_reader_extract_iter_read(
                                iter2,
                                buf.as_mut_ptr() as *mut c_void,
                                buf.len(),
                            );
                            if n == 0 {
                                break;
                            }
                            total_iter = total_iter.wrapping_add(n as u64);
                            digest = fold(digest, bytes_checksum(&buf[..n]));
                        }
                        digest = fold(digest, total_iter);
                        let fr = zip::mz_zip_reader_extract_iter_free(iter2);
                        digest = fold(digest, fr as u64);
                    }

                    let mut no_alloc = vec![0u8; buf_cap];
                    let mut user_buf = vec![0u8; 8192];
                    let exna = zip::mz_zip_reader_extract_to_mem_no_alloc(
                        pzip,
                        qidx,
                        no_alloc.as_mut_ptr() as *mut c_void,
                        no_alloc.len(),
                        0,
                        user_buf.as_mut_ptr() as *mut c_void,
                        user_buf.len(),
                    );
                    digest = fold(digest, exna as u64);

                    let exf_mem = zip::mz_zip_reader_extract_file_to_mem(
                        pzip,
                        name.as_ptr() as *const c_char,
                        no_alloc.as_mut_ptr() as *mut c_void,
                        no_alloc.len(),
                        0,
                    );
                    digest = fold(digest, exf_mem as u64);

                    let exf_na = zip::mz_zip_reader_extract_file_to_mem_no_alloc(
                        pzip,
                        name.as_ptr() as *const c_char,
                        no_alloc.as_mut_ptr() as *mut c_void,
                        no_alloc.len(),
                        0,
                        user_buf.as_mut_ptr() as *mut c_void,
                        user_buf.len(),
                    );
                    digest = fold(digest, exf_na as u64);

                    let mut heap2_len = 0usize;
                    let heap2 = zip::mz_zip_reader_extract_file_to_heap(
                        pzip,
                        name.as_ptr() as *const c_char,
                        &mut heap2_len,
                        0,
                    );
                    digest = fold(digest, heap2_len as u64);
                    if !heap2.is_null() {
                        let h = slice::from_raw_parts(heap2 as *const u8, heap2_len);
                        digest = fold(digest, bytes_checksum(h));
                        mz::mz_free(heap2);
                    }

                    let mut cb = ZipCbState::default();
                    let exf_cb = zip::mz_zip_reader_extract_file_to_callback(
                        pzip,
                        name.as_ptr() as *const c_char,
                        Some(zip_write_cb),
                        &mut cb as *mut _ as *mut c_void,
                        0,
                    );
                    digest = fold(digest, exf_cb as u64);
                    digest = fold(digest, cb.total);
                    digest = fold(digest, cb.calls);
                    digest = fold(digest, cb.digest);
                }

                last_err_code = zip::mz_zip_get_last_error(pzip) as u64;
                digest = fold(digest, last_err_code);
                digest = fold(digest, cstr_len(zip::mz_zip_get_error_string(last_err_code as _)));

                let _ = zip::mz_zip_reader_end(pzip);
                let _ = zip::mz_zip_end(pzip);
            } else {
                let e = zip::mz_zip_get_last_error(pzip) as u64;
                last_err_code = e;
                digest = fold(digest, e);
                digest = fold(digest, cstr_len(zip::mz_zip_get_error_string(e as _)));
                let _ = zip::mz_zip_end(pzip);
            }
        }
    }

    format!("op=zip_reader_blob err={} digest={:016x}", last_err_code, digest)
}

fn zip_file_ops(input: &[u8], iters: u64) -> String {
    let mut digest = 0u64;
    let mut last_err = 0u64;

    for i in 0..iters {
        let base = format!("miniz_raw_harness_{}_{}", input.len(), i);
        let dir = std::env::temp_dir().join(base);
        let _ = fs::create_dir_all(&dir);

        let zip_path = dir.join("archive.zip");
        let src_path = dir.join("src.bin");
        let out1_path = dir.join("out1.bin");
        let out2_path = dir.join("out2.bin");
        let out3_path = dir.join("out3.bin");

        let _ = fs::write(&src_path, input);

        unsafe {
            let c_zip = CString::new(zip_path.to_string_lossy().as_bytes()).ok();
            let c_src = CString::new(src_path.to_string_lossy().as_bytes()).ok();
            let c_out1 = CString::new(out1_path.to_string_lossy().as_bytes()).ok();
            let c_out2 = CString::new(out2_path.to_string_lossy().as_bytes()).ok();
            let c_out3 = CString::new(out3_path.to_string_lossy().as_bytes()).ok();
            let c_arc1 = CString::new("alpha.txt").ok();
            let c_arc2 = CString::new("beta.bin").ok();
            let c_arc3 = CString::new("cb.dat").ok();

            if c_zip.is_none()
                || c_src.is_none()
                || c_out1.is_none()
                || c_out2.is_none()
                || c_out3.is_none()
                || c_arc1.is_none()
                || c_arc2.is_none()
                || c_arc3.is_none()
            {
                digest = fold(digest, 1);
                continue;
            }

            let c_zip = c_zip.unwrap();
            let c_src = c_src.unwrap();
            let c_out1 = c_out1.unwrap();
            let c_out2 = c_out2.unwrap();
            let c_out3 = c_out3.unwrap();
            let c_arc1 = c_arc1.unwrap();
            let c_arc2 = c_arc2.unwrap();
            let c_arc3 = c_arc3.unwrap();

            let mut za = MaybeUninit::<zip::mz_zip_archive>::zeroed();
            let pzip = za.as_mut_ptr();
            zip::mz_zip_zero_struct(pzip);

            let winit = zip::mz_zip_writer_init_file_v2(pzip, c_zip.as_ptr(), 0, 0);
            digest = fold(digest, winit as u64);
            if winit != 0 {
                digest = fold(digest, zip::mz_zip_get_mode(pzip) as u64);
                digest = fold(digest, zip::mz_zip_get_type(pzip) as u64);

                let addf = zip::mz_zip_writer_add_file(
                    pzip,
                    c_arc1.as_ptr(),
                    c_src.as_ptr(),
                    ptr::null(),
                    0,
                    6,
                );
                digest = fold(digest, addf as u64);

                let addm = zip::mz_zip_writer_add_mem_ex_v2(
                    pzip,
                    c_arc2.as_ptr(),
                    if input.is_empty() { ptr::null() } else { input.as_ptr() as *const c_void },
                    input.len(),
                    b"comment\0".as_ptr() as *const c_void,
                    7,
                    6,
                    0,
                    0,
                    ptr::null_mut(),
                    ptr::null(),
                    0,
                    ptr::null(),
                    0,
                );
                digest = fold(digest, addm as u64);

                let mut rstate = ReadBufState {
                    data: input,
                    total: 0,
                    calls: 0,
                    digest: 0,
                };
                let addcb = zip::mz_zip_writer_add_read_buf_callback(
                    pzip,
                    c_arc3.as_ptr(),
                    Some(read_buf_cb),
                    &mut rstate as *mut _ as *mut c_void,
                    input.len() as u64,
                    ptr::null(),
                    ptr::null(),
                    0,
                    6,
                    ptr::null(),
                    0,
                    ptr::null(),
                    0,
                );
                digest = fold(digest, addcb as u64);
                digest = fold(digest, rstate.total);
                digest = fold(digest, rstate.calls);
                digest = fold(digest, rstate.digest);

                let fin = zip::mz_zip_writer_finalize_archive(pzip);
                digest = fold(digest, fin as u64);
                let _ = zip::mz_zip_writer_end(pzip);
            } else {
                let _ = zip::mz_zip_writer_end(pzip);
            }

            let mut verr: zip::mz_zip_error = 0;
            let vfa = zip::mz_zip_validate_file_archive(c_zip.as_ptr(), 0, &mut verr);
            digest = fold(digest, vfa as u64);
            digest = fold(digest, verr as u64);

            let mut ext_len = 0usize;
            let ext = zip::mz_zip_extract_archive_file_to_heap(c_zip.as_ptr(), c_arc1.as_ptr(), &mut ext_len, 0);
            digest = fold(digest, ext_len as u64);
            if !ext.is_null() {
                let b = slice::from_raw_parts(ext as *const u8, ext_len);
                digest = fold(digest, bytes_checksum(b));
                mz::mz_free(ext);
            }

            let mut ext2_len = 0usize;
            let mut err2: zip::mz_zip_error = 0;
            let ext2 = zip::mz_zip_extract_archive_file_to_heap_v2(
                c_zip.as_ptr(),
                c_arc2.as_ptr(),
                ptr::null(),
                &mut ext2_len,
                0,
                &mut err2,
            );
            digest = fold(digest, ext2_len as u64);
            digest = fold(digest, err2 as u64);
            if !ext2.is_null() {
                let b = slice::from_raw_parts(ext2 as *const u8, ext2_len);
                digest = fold(digest, bytes_checksum(b));
                mz::mz_free(ext2);
            }

            let add_in_place = zip::mz_zip_add_mem_to_archive_file_in_place(
                c_zip.as_ptr(),
                CString::new("delta.txt").unwrap().as_ptr(),
                if input.is_empty() { ptr::null() } else { input.as_ptr() as *const c_void },
                input.len(),
                ptr::null(),
                0,
                6,
            );
            digest = fold(digest, add_in_place as u64);

            let mut err3: zip::mz_zip_error = 0;
            let add_in_place2 = zip::mz_zip_add_mem_to_archive_file_in_place_v2(
                c_zip.as_ptr(),
                CString::new("epsilon.txt").unwrap().as_ptr(),
                if input.is_empty() { ptr::null() } else { input.as_ptr() as *const c_void },
                input.len(),
                ptr::null(),
                0,
                6,
                &mut err3,
            );
            digest = fold(digest, add_in_place2 as u64);
            digest = fold(digest, err3 as u64);

            let mut zr = MaybeUninit::<zip::mz_zip_archive>::zeroed();
            let prz = zr.as_mut_ptr();
            zip::mz_zip_zero_struct(prz);
            let rinit = zip::mz_zip_reader_init_file(prz, c_zip.as_ptr(), 0);
            digest = fold(digest, rinit as u64);
            if rinit != 0 {
                let num = zip::mz_zip_reader_get_num_files(prz);
                digest = fold(digest, num as u64);

                let exf = zip::mz_zip_reader_extract_file_to_file(prz, c_arc1.as_ptr(), c_out1.as_ptr(), 0);
                digest = fold(digest, exf as u64);

                let loc = zip::mz_zip_reader_locate_file(prz, c_arc2.as_ptr(), ptr::null(), 0);
                digest = fold(digest, loc as u64);
                if loc >= 0 {
                    let exi = zip::mz_zip_reader_extract_to_file(prz, loc as u32, c_out2.as_ptr(), 0);
                    digest = fold(digest, exi as u64);
                }

                let _ = zip::mz_zip_reader_end(prz);
                let _ = zip::mz_zip_end(prz);
            } else {
                let _ = zip::mz_zip_end(prz);
            }

            let mut zr2 = MaybeUninit::<zip::mz_zip_archive>::zeroed();
            let prz2 = zr2.as_mut_ptr();
            zip::mz_zip_zero_struct(prz2);
            let rinit2 = zip::mz_zip_reader_init_file_v2(prz2, c_zip.as_ptr(), 0, 0, 0);
            digest = fold(digest, rinit2 as u64);
            if rinit2 != 0 {
                let loc = zip::mz_zip_reader_locate_file(prz2, c_arc3.as_ptr(), ptr::null(), 0);
                digest = fold(digest, loc as u64);
                if loc >= 0 {
                    let exi = zip::mz_zip_reader_extract_to_file(prz2, loc as u32, c_out3.as_ptr(), 0);
                    digest = fold(digest, exi as u64);
                }
                last_err = zip::mz_zip_get_last_error(prz2) as u64;
                digest = fold(digest, last_err);
                let _ = zip::mz_zip_reader_end(prz2);
                let _ = zip::mz_zip_end(prz2);
            } else {
                last_err = zip::mz_zip_get_last_error(prz2) as u64;
                digest = fold(digest, last_err);
                let _ = zip::mz_zip_end(prz2);
            }

            if let Ok(b) = fs::read(&zip_path) {
                digest = fold(digest, bytes_checksum(&b));
            }
            if let Ok(b) = fs::read(&out1_path) {
                digest = fold(digest, bytes_checksum(&b));
            }
            if let Ok(b) = fs::read(&out2_path) {
                digest = fold(digest, bytes_checksum(&b));
            }
            if let Ok(b) = fs::read(&out3_path) {
                digest = fold(digest, bytes_checksum(&b));
            }

            let mut st = MaybeUninit::<zip::stat64>::zeroed();
            let src_stat = zip::stat64(c_src.as_ptr(), st.as_mut_ptr());
            digest = fold(digest, src_stat as u64);
            let zip_stat = zip::stat64(c_zip.as_ptr(), st.as_mut_ptr());
            digest = fold(digest, zip_stat as u64);
        }

        let _ = fs::remove_file(&zip_path);
        let _ = fs::remove_file(&src_path);
        let _ = fs::remove_file(&out1_path);
        let _ = fs::remove_file(&out2_path);
        let _ = fs::remove_file(&out3_path);
        let _ = fs::remove_dir_all(&dir);
    }

    format!("op=zip_file_ops err={} digest={:016x}", last_err, digest)
}

pub fn ops() -> Vec<(&'static str, fn(&[u8], u64) -> String)> {
    vec![
        ("mz_stream_roundtrip", mz_stream_roundtrip as fn(&[u8], u64) -> String),
        ("tinfl_decode_blob", tinfl_decode_blob as fn(&[u8], u64) -> String),
        ("tdefl_encode_blob", tdefl_encode_blob as fn(&[u8], u64) -> String),
        ("zip_mem_roundtrip", zip_mem_roundtrip as fn(&[u8], u64) -> String),
        ("zip_reader_blob", zip_reader_blob as fn(&[u8], u64) -> String),
        ("zip_file_ops", zip_file_ops as fn(&[u8], u64) -> String),
    ]
}

pub fn gen_seeds(dir: &str) -> Vec<String> {
    let _ = fs::create_dir_all(dir);
    let mut lines = Vec::new();

    let raw1 = make_text_payload(160);
    let raw2 = make_mixed_payload(150);

    for (op, idx, bytes) in [
        ("mz_stream_roundtrip", 1usize, raw1.as_slice()),
        ("mz_stream_roundtrip", 2usize, raw2.as_slice()),
        ("tdefl_encode_blob", 1usize, raw1.as_slice()),
        ("tdefl_encode_blob", 2usize, raw2.as_slice()),
        ("zip_mem_roundtrip", 1usize, raw1.as_slice()),
        ("zip_mem_roundtrip", 2usize, raw2.as_slice()),
        ("zip_file_ops", 1usize, raw1.as_slice()),
        ("zip_file_ops", 2usize, raw2.as_slice()),
    ] {
        let path = format!("{}/{}.{}.bin", dir, op, idx);
        if write_file(&path, bytes) {
            lines.push(format!("seed {} {}", op, path));
        }
    }

    let comp1 = compress_zlib_blob(&raw1, 6)
        .unwrap_or_else(|| Vec::from(&b"x\x9c\x03\x00\x00\x00\x00\x01"[..]));
    let comp2 = compress_zlib_blob(&raw2, 6)
        .unwrap_or_else(|| Vec::from(&b"x\x9c\x03\x00\x00\x00\x00\x01"[..]));
    for (idx, bytes) in [(1usize, comp1.as_slice()), (2usize, comp2.as_slice())] {
        let path = format!("{}/tinfl_decode_blob.{}.bin", dir, idx);
        if write_file(&path, bytes) {
            lines.push(format!("seed tinfl_decode_blob {}", path));
        }
    }

    let z1_members = [
        (raw1[..raw1.len().min(4096)].as_ref(), b"alpha.txt\0".as_slice(), None),
        (raw2[..raw2.len().min(2048)].as_ref(), b"beta.bin\0".as_slice(), Some(b"beta-comment".as_slice())),
        (raw1[..raw1.len().min(1024)].as_ref(), b"gamma/log.json\0".as_slice(), Some(b"gamma-comment".as_slice())),
    ];
    let z2_members = [
        (raw2[..raw2.len().min(3500)].as_ref(), b"alpha.txt\0".as_slice(), None),
        (raw1[..raw1.len().min(2800)].as_ref(), b"beta.bin\0".as_slice(), Some(b"beta-comment-2".as_slice())),
        (raw2[..raw2.len().min(1500)].as_ref(), b"gamma/log.json\0".as_slice(), Some(b"gamma-comment-2".as_slice())),
    ];

    let zip1 = build_zip_blob(&z1_members).or_else(|| {
        build_zip_blob(&[
            (b"seed alpha\n".as_ref(), b"alpha.txt\0".as_slice(), None),
            (b"\x00\x01\x02seed-beta".as_ref(), b"beta.bin\0".as_slice(), None),
            (b"{\"k\":\"v1\"}\n".as_ref(), b"gamma/log.json\0".as_slice(), None),
        ])
    });
    let zip2 = build_zip_blob(&z2_members).or_else(|| {
        build_zip_blob(&[
            (b"another deterministic alpha payload\n".as_ref(), b"alpha.txt\0".as_slice(), None),
            (b"\x10\x20\x30\x40different-beta".as_ref(), b"beta.bin\0".as_slice(), None),
            (b"{\"k\":\"v2\",\"n\":2}\n".as_ref(), b"gamma/log.json\0".as_slice(), None),
        ])
    });

    if let Some(bytes) = zip1 {
        let path = format!("{}/zip_reader_blob.1.bin", dir);
        if write_file(&path, &bytes) {
            lines.push(format!("seed zip_reader_blob {}", path));
        }
    }
    if let Some(bytes) = zip2 {
        let path = format!("{}/zip_reader_blob.2.bin", dir);
        if write_file(&path, &bytes) {
            lines.push(format!("seed zip_reader_blob {}", path));
        }
    }

    lines
}

pub fn gen_perf(dir: &str) -> Vec<String> {
    let _ = fs::create_dir_all(dir);
    let mut lines = Vec::new();

    let raw = make_perf_payload();

    let p1 = format!("{}/mz_stream_roundtrip.perf.bin", dir);
    if write_file(&p1, &raw) {
        lines.push(format!("perf mz_stream_roundtrip {}", p1));
    }

    let p2 = format!("{}/tdefl_encode_blob.perf.bin", dir);
    if write_file(&p2, &raw) {
        lines.push(format!("perf tdefl_encode_blob {}", p2));
    }

    let p3 = format!("{}/zip_mem_roundtrip.perf.bin", dir);
    if write_file(&p3, &raw) {
        lines.push(format!("perf zip_mem_roundtrip {}", p3));
    }

    let p4 = format!("{}/zip_file_ops.perf.bin", dir);
    if write_file(&p4, &raw) {
        lines.push(format!("perf zip_file_ops {}", p4));
    }

    if let Some(comp) = compress_zlib_blob(&raw, 6) {
        let p5 = format!("{}/tinfl_decode_blob.perf.bin", dir);
        if write_file(&p5, &comp) {
            lines.push(format!("perf tinfl_decode_blob {}", p5));
        }
    }

    let n = raw.len();
    let a_end = n.min(2_000_000);
    let b_start = n / 5;
    let b_len = n.min(1_500_000);
    let b_end = b_start.saturating_add(b_len).min(n);
    let c_start = n / 2;

    let members = [
        (raw[..a_end].as_ref(), b"alpha.txt\0".as_slice(), None),
        (raw[b_start..b_end].as_ref(), b"beta.bin\0".as_slice(), Some(b"perf-beta".as_slice())),
        (raw[c_start..].as_ref(), b"gamma/log.json\0".as_slice(), Some(b"perf-gamma".as_slice())),
    ];
    if let Some(zip_bytes) = build_zip_blob(&members) {
        let p6 = format!("{}/zip_reader_blob.perf.bin", dir);
        if write_file(&p6, &zip_bytes) {
            lines.push(format!("perf zip_reader_blob {}", p6));
        }
    }

    lines
}
